<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="utf-8">
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
  <title>{{title}}</title>
  <link rel="stylesheet" href="/css/style.css">
</head>
<body>
  {{> header}}

  <main>
    <section class="hero">
      <div class="shell hero-grid">
        <div>
          <p class="eyebrow">Travel planning made simple</p>
          <h1>Discover your next getaway.</h1>
          <p class="hero-copy">
            Browse travel packages backed by the Travlr REST API and MongoDB database.
            Administrators can securely manage trip inventory through the Angular dashboard.
          </p>
          <div class="actions">
            <a class="button primary" href="/travel">Browse trips</a>
            <a class="button secondary" href="http://localhost:4200" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open admin</a>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="hero-art" aria-hidden="true">
          <div class="sun"></div>
          <div class="wave wave-one"></div>
          <div class="wave wave-two"></div>
          <span>TRAVLR</span>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="shell feature-section">
      <article class="feature-card">
        <h2>Dynamic trip data</h2>
        <p>Travel packages are loaded through the Express REST API instead of being hardcoded into the page.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="feature-card">
        <h2>MongoDB persistence</h2>
        <p>Mongoose models provide structured access to trip and administrator account data.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="feature-card">
        <h2>Protected administration</h2>
        <p>JWT authentication and Passport middleware protect trip creation, editing, and deletion.</p>
      </article>
    </section>
  </main>

  {{> footer}}
</body>
</html>
